1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,615
While there may be some really cool ideas that come up in a sprint,

2
00:00:03,615 --> 00:00:06,630
you'll need to select one to move forward with.

3
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:10,485
There's always going to be trade-offs to be made when building products.

4
00:00:10,485 --> 00:00:14,580
Using a decision matrix is an easy way to visualize the tradeoffs,

5
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:17,610
have different ideas against specific criteria.

6
00:00:17,610 --> 00:00:21,660
You'll go through this exercise together as a team and discuss and

7
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:26,025
agree on where each idea falls against the criteria that you've selected.

8
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:29,820
Most commonly, the criteria is value versus effort,

9
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:34,730
but it's possible to further define these into more specific criteria.

10
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:37,010
For example, new users,

11
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:38,525
reduction in user pain,

12
00:00:38,525 --> 00:00:43,130
or competitive advantage for value and things like time,

13
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:46,955
cost and dependencies on other teams for effort.

14
00:00:46,955 --> 00:00:50,915
Here's an example of what a decision matrix looks like.

15
00:00:50,915 --> 00:00:57,140
Along the x-axis you have user value and along the y-axis you have effort.

16
00:00:57,140 --> 00:01:00,620
Each quadrant then represents a different combination of

17
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:05,570
user value for the given idea and the effort required to build it.

18
00:01:05,570 --> 00:01:10,115
The lower left quadrant is low value low effort.

19
00:01:10,115 --> 00:01:15,425
Ideas that fall here don't provide a ton of user value but,

20
00:01:15,425 --> 00:01:18,635
they also don't require a ton of effort to build either.

21
00:01:18,635 --> 00:01:25,670
An example of an idea that would fall into this category is the Facebook poke feature.

22
00:01:25,670 --> 00:01:27,620
It's a really simple feature,

23
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:31,565
but it didn't really produce a lot of value for users.

24
00:01:31,565 --> 00:01:35,915
The upper left quadrant is low value high effort.

25
00:01:35,915 --> 00:01:39,835
Ideas here don't provide a ton of user value,

26
00:01:39,835 --> 00:01:43,265
but they require a ton of effort to build.

27
00:01:43,265 --> 00:01:48,140
Usually, it doesn't make sense to pursue these ideas and they should be avoided.

28
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:52,870
An example of an idea that would fall into this category is juice seller.

29
00:01:52,870 --> 00:01:56,030
You might have heard of this startup but they built

30
00:01:56,030 --> 00:02:00,665
a $400 internet-connected machine for cold pressing juice.

31
00:02:00,665 --> 00:02:04,610
You'd subscribe to a monthly plan and get juice packs delivered,

32
00:02:04,610 --> 00:02:07,840
then you'd put them into the machine and it would press the juice out.

33
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:13,865
However, users quickly found out that eventually the machine wasn't even really needed.

34
00:02:13,865 --> 00:02:17,210
You could just use your hands to squeeze the juice out of the packs.

35
00:02:17,210 --> 00:02:20,300
It was a pointless product that didn't solve a real need for

36
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:23,780
users and eventually the company shut down as a result.

37
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:25,525
You don't want to do this,

38
00:02:25,525 --> 00:02:28,100
you definitely don't want to build this type of product.

39
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:30,485
So try to avoid these ideas.

40
00:02:30,485 --> 00:02:34,925
The lower right quadrant is high value low effort.

41
00:02:34,925 --> 00:02:40,460
Ideas here provide lots of user value and don't require a ton of effort to build.

42
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:44,060
These types of ideas are usually worth investing in,

43
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:48,650
but keep in mind that if it doesn't take you a lot of effort to build,

44
00:02:48,650 --> 00:02:52,655
it likely won't take other companies a ton of effort to build either.

45
00:02:52,655 --> 00:02:57,020
An example of an idea that fits into this category is banks offering

46
00:02:57,020 --> 00:03:01,700
the ability for you to toggle your debit or credit card on and off through their app.

47
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:04,160
This provides you with the flexibility to

48
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,680
disable your card if you think you might have lost it,

49
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:11,630
or if you want to prevent it from being used without having to call and cancel the card.

50
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:16,780
You can then easily re-enable it when you find it or you're ready to make a purchase.

51
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:21,260
The upper right quadrant is high value high effort.

52
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:27,080
Ideas here provide tons of user value but also require a lot of effort to build.

53
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:31,420
This is another area where it's worth investing in these types of ideas.

54
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:34,440
An example would be Gmail.

55
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,430
When Gmail first launched,

56
00:03:36,430 --> 00:03:40,490
it provided a crazy amount of storage for free.

57
00:03:40,490 --> 00:03:45,830
Gmail also has an amazing spam filtering system to keep unwanted messages out of

58
00:03:45,830 --> 00:03:50,929
your inbox and it introduced a new mental model for how to organize,

59
00:03:50,929 --> 00:03:54,845
store and find your emails through labeling, archiving and searching.

60
00:03:54,845 --> 00:03:58,475
Each one of those things is a massive undertaking.

61
00:03:58,475 --> 00:04:00,650
After going through this exercise,

62
00:04:00,650 --> 00:04:04,325
you might find some ideas that are high value low effort,

63
00:04:04,325 --> 00:04:07,460
or high value high effort.

64
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:10,955
These are the best types of ideas that are worth pursuing.

65
00:04:10,955 --> 00:04:15,650
You might also find some ideas that are low value low effort and

66
00:04:15,650 --> 00:04:18,020
sometimes it can be worth pursuing these ideas if

67
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:21,065
there's nothing more impactful that the team can be doing.

68
00:04:21,065 --> 00:04:26,840
Lastly, you might find some ideas that are low value high effort ideas.

69
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:31,040
Generally, it will never make sense to pursue those types of ideas.

70
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:34,370
Remember just because you don't pursue an idea right

71
00:04:34,370 --> 00:04:39,120
now doesn't mean that you can't pursue it at some point in the future.

